    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d731-a2">

                <pb facs="0727" n="1461" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1461"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-12-21"><hi rendition="#small-caps">December</hi> 21,
                            1895</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: Since writing on the 19th, I have
                    learned that Mr. Martin’s fear for our safety at present arises from the fact
                    that the Kol Aghase Haji Halil Effendi does not work in harmony with the
                    kaimakam, Ismael Bey. So far as we can learn, the kaimakam is in the right every
                    time when any difference arises between them. The other has said more than once
                    that the kaimakamluk of Ismael Bey is only a three days’ affair.</p>
                <p>Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. L. Coffing.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
